12
01:06:56,842 --> 01:07:02,842
Fatherland is a 1994 American alternate history mystery-thriller film directed by Christopher Menaul, written by Stanley Weiser
and Ron Hutchinson, and starring Rutger Hauer, Miranda Richardson, Peter Vaughan, Jean Marsh and Michael Kitchen.

13
01:12:31,578 --> 01:12:37,578
Based on the 1992 novel by Robert Harris, the film is set in an alternate 1960s Germany still
under Nazi control, and concerns a murder investigation of Party officials.

14
01:18:06,315 --> 01:18:12,315
The film premiered on HBO on November 26, 1994.

15
01:23:41,052 --> 01:23:47,052
It received mixed reviews, but was a commercial success.

16
01:29:15,789 --> 01:29:21,789
Miranda Richardson won a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress – Miniseries or Television Film, while the film was also nominated
for Best Limited or Anthology Series or Television Film and Best Actor – Miniseries or Television Film (for Hauer).

17
01:34:50,526 --> 01:34:56,526
The film explores themes of journalist, nazi, ss (nazi
schutzstaffel), holocaust (shoah), murder hunt.

18
01:40:25,263 --> 01:40:31,263
The tone is emotional and intense.
